============================================================================
(1) ADJOINT IDENTITY  <h*a,b> = <a,h@b>  on Z/N  (complex, random)
============================================================================
  N= 7: |<h*a,b>-<a,h@b>| = 3.58e-15   |h@b-(sigma h-bar)*b| = 0.00e+00
  N=12: |<h*a,b>-<a,h@b>| = 7.11e-15   |h@b-(sigma h-bar)*b| = 0.00e+00
  N=27: |<h*a,b>-<a,h@b>| = 4.77e-14   |h@b-(sigma h-bar)*b| = 7.80e-15
  => cross-correlation IS the adjoint of convolution; the link is the antipodal sigma (S702).

============================================================================
(2) LRC speed set: convolution=SUMSET (shell, 2n-1) vs correlation=DIFFs (clock, n)
============================================================================
  S=[1, 2, 3, 5, 12], n=6: clock modulus n=6, shell modulus 2n-1=11
  SUMSET (convolution 1_S*1_S) support sizes: 13 distinct sums; shell-partners a+b==0 mod 11: []
  DIFFSET (correlation 1_S@1_S) is symmetric (d and -d): {1: 2, 2: 2, 3: 1, 4: 1, 7: 1, 9: 1, 10: 1, 11: 1}
  conv==sumset-mult: True;  corr==diff-mult: True

============================================================================
(3) ADDITIVE ENERGY two ways: ||1_S@1_S||^2 (space) == sum |hat 1_S|^4 (Fourier)
============================================================================
  S=[1, 2, 3, 5, 12]: E(space ||auto||^2)=53  E(Fourier sum|F|^4/N)=53.000  E(direct #a+b=c+d)=53
  S=[0, 1, 2, 3, 4]: E(space ||auto||^2)=85  E(Fourier sum|F|^4/N)=85.000  E(direct #a+b=c+d)=85
  S=[1, 3, 4, 9, 11]: E(space ||auto||^2)=53  E(Fourier sum|F|^4/N)=53.000  E(direct #a+b=c+d)=53
  => additive energy = ||autocorrelation||^2 = 4th Fourier moment (Wiener-Khinchin).
     This is exactly the repo's unit-distance/Cayley additive-energy object (S599).

============================================================================
(4) TOURNAMENT: converse = adjoint of circulant adjacency; self-converse=self-adjoint
============================================================================
  C_5: converse conn set -H=[3, 4] (vs H=[1, 2]); symbol(A^T)=conj(symbol(A)): 6.3e-16; skew S*=-S: 0.0e+00; self-converse(multiplier): True
  C_7: converse conn set -H=[4, 5, 6] (vs H=[1, 2, 3]); symbol(A^T)=conj(symbol(A)): 8.5e-15; skew S*=-S: 0.0e+00; self-converse(multiplier): True
  => converse T* = A^T = adjoint of the adjacency-convolution; self-converse worry-set
     (THM-402) = self-adjoint-up-to-multiplier; the {+-1} skew-adjacency is skew-Hermitian.

